      <chord name="Eb"/>Not I, <chord name="Bb7"/>but <chord name="Eb"/>Christ, <chord name="Ab"/>in <chord name="Bb7"/>every thought and <chord name="Eb"/>word.
      </lines>
    </verse>
    <verse name="v2">
      <lines>
      <chord name="Eb"/>Not <chord name="Bb7"/>I, but <chord name="Eb"/>Christ, to <chord name="Bb7"/>gently soothe <chord name="Eb"/>in sorrow,<br/>
      <chord name="Ab"/>Not <chord name="Eb"/>I, but <chord name="Bb7"/>Christ, to <chord name="Eb"/>wipe the <chord name="Bb"/>falling tear;<br/>
      <chord name="Eb"/>Not <chord name="Bb7"/>I, but <chord name="Cm7"/>Christ, <chord name="Bb7"/>to lift <chord name="Ab"/>the <chord name="Eb"/>weary burden,<br/>
      <chord name="Eb"/>Not <chord name="Bb7"/>I, but <chord name="Eb"/>Christ, <chord name="Ab"/>to hush <chord name="Bb7"/>away <chord name="Eb"/>all fear.
      </lines>
    </verse>
    <verse name="v3">
      <lines>
      <chord name="Eb"/>Christ, <chord name="Bb7"/>only Christ! <chord name="Eb"/>No <chord name="Bb7"/>idle words <chord name="Eb"/>e&#x27;er falling,<br/>
      <chord name="Ab"/>Christ, <chord name="Eb"/>only <chord name="Bb7"/>Christ; no <chord name="Eb"/>needless <chord name="Bb"/>bustling sound;<br/>
      <chord name="Eb"/>Christ, <chord name="Bb7"/>only <chord name="Cm7"/>Christ, <chord name="Bb7"/>no <chord name="Ab"/>self <chord name="Eb"/>important bearing;<br/>
      <chord name="Eb"/>Christ, <chord name="Bb7"/>only Christ, <chord name="Eb"/>no <chord name="Ab"/>trace of <chord name="Bb7"/>&quot;I&quot; <chord name="Eb"/>be found.
      </lines>
